Wrote the label file: one row for `abortion`, coded BLANK `no-evidence`. Both sources trace to SB1457 (2021), which Lieberman voted No on as a state representative — but the bill's content (selective-abortion ban by reason, an educational-facility restriction, clinic/informed-consent rules) is off-axis to the ladder's gestational-stage/exception dimension, so neither passage clears V2 to support a chair.
